    "description": "Backup Sight Rail (FGC-9 MK1): Laffs Dynamics\n\nA picatinny rail for the legacy model FGC-9 MK1, designed with built in low profile iron sights, should a user not currently have a weapon \noptic, or their current optic ceases to function. Useful for ranges between 0 - 30 meters. \n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .12\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 7+\nInfill: 80%+\n\n\n\nNotes:\n\n1) This data pack is just for printing the handguard. To get the base firearm data pack, use the following link: \n(https://odysee.com/@TheGatalog-HybridDesigns:0/FGC-9:e)\n\n\n\nCredit:\n\nJStark1809, IvanTheTroll, 3socksandcrocs; Creators of the FGC-9 MKI, used the picatinny rail geometry as a base for creating this design. ",
